you're playing William Hartnell the  first doctor and adventure in space and  time what does it feel like to be taking  on such a huge role as that well I I  didn't realize when I took it on that  the amount of interest there would be  all I knew is that Mark invited me to do  it just over a year ago and I just said  yes very quickly before he changed his  mind and because I remember William  Hartnell and not only is Doctor Who but  as one of our finest character screen  actors in the 50s and 60s so I knew of  him and I knew his work so I felt I felt  a big sense of responsibility not only  to to honor his memory and for a sake of  his family but also as a man and also as  an actor I saw the script and I thought  this is something special but you never  know how film turns out and sometimes  you do things and if they don't turn out  as you'd imagined either for better or  for worse but this the response to this  adventure in space and time that they're  in the cinema screening the other day  when I saw it was absolutely amazing I  think everyone was very moved and  untouched by the way the fans took to it  because we wanted it to be right with  all the fans because you know they've  followed the series I mean for 50 years  it did feel quite a responsibility as I  said and we hope that when it finally  goes on there later this week that the  fans will will take to it and think  we've done a good job absolutely sure  they will do it had a rapturous applause  so far from the screening at the BFI of  course this leads us into the  anniversary special which leads us into  the new doctor later in the year what do  you think of the choice of Peter Capaldi  as the next Doctor well when we were  part way through the filming  Peter pay the studio visit  because seizing a friend of Mount Gators  and not invited him to come along  because he asked if he could because I  spoke to him I've never met him before  what a delightful guy he was and I  realized he was a lifelong Doctor